{
  "description": "Talksasa Pay webhook signature test vectors. Generated independently (Python hmac) and checked by the Go (pkg/talksasapay) and PHP SDK tests. Canonical copy: pkg/talksasapay/testdata/webhook_signature_vectors.json.",
  "algorithm": [
    "Header: Talksasa-Signature: t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex>[,v1=<hex>...]",
    "Parse: split on ',', trim spaces/tabs around each item, split at the first '='. Exactly one t (1-12 ASCII digits). v1 values that are not 64 hex digits are ignored; at least one well-formed v1 is required. Other keys are ignored. An item without '=' (or with an empty key) is malformed.",
    "Timestamp: reject if |now - t| > tolerance (300 s), both directions; |now - t| == tolerance is accepted.",
    "signed_payload = <t as sent> + '.' + <raw body bytes, unmodified>",
    "expected = lowercase hex(HMAC-SHA256(key = UTF-8 bytes of the full secret string incl. 'whsec_', message = signed_payload))",
    "Accept if any v1 (lowercased) equals expected for any configured secret, compared in constant time."
  ],
  "reasons": [
    "missing_header",
    "malformed_header",
    "timestamp_out_of_tolerance",
    "no_matching_signature"
  ],
